LAST_SUCCESS=Task 97 bug#1 FIXED + device-verified — host call-output silence pump. spawn_call_silence_pump (audio_impl.rs, spawned from guest create_track VoiceCall path): per-track thread, every 5ms (1) ALWAYS drains up-queue (suspend can't latch) + (2) only when guest silent >25ms, tops ring to ~1/2 capacity with silence (mixer never underflows→no XRUN flood→no suspend). Guest-vs-pump distinguished by TrackState.last_guest_write_ns (set only by guest write_pcm_f32); ring_write() extracted + shared. A/B verified (--probe-call-stall 5 1 0 <pump>): pump OFF→up_fill 0→128, r froze @252ms, "Suspending stream what=3"; pump ON→up_fill 0, r advanced whole stall window, no suspend, no fighting on resume (cum_zero=0).
NOTES=Bug #3 (guest UI idle freeze) STILL SEPARATE/OPEN — the pump keeps the AUDIO stream alive through a guest stall (no relaunch needed) but the guest UI still needs its own wake-up fix. Scoped pump to VoiceCall only (Media/Notification feed themselves). Probe opens via open_routed (pump-free) so it still reproduces. Earpiece pin [2] -889s standalone (taimen, bug#5); verified on speaker [3]. Device probe binary: /data/local/tmp/wart-host-probe97. Next candidates: bug#3 guest wake, bug#5 route-toggle reliability, bug#2 audioserver degrade triggers.
